## 8 October 2026: Clear native panel and truthful menu-bar proof

The popover draws an opaque system window color, so app content behind it cannot reduce text contrast. The seven fixtures assert this through `contentOpaque`. (8 October 2026)

`NSStatusItem.isVisible` and Accessibility availability do not prove the icon is physically visible: macOS can hide an item when the menu bar runs out of room. Check an actual menu-bar screenshot after installation; the current compact button remains registered, but its placement outside the overflow group is not yet proven. (8 October 2026)

The status item's `autosaveName` is `com.zenray.assets.dashboard.status`, which lets macOS preserve a position after the item is moved. A stable name alone does not move it out of overflow. (8 October 2026)

